sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, one Swamp run, certificate signing is the one step-to-Gateway call. docs/reference/analytics.md#publish-a-tracking-host.
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: instance:analytics:enable
  %% kind: analytics.enable
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane P icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as Serving Node<br/>Instance or Router
  participant P as Plausible<br/>analytics role
  CLI->>GW: instance:analytics:enable<br/>INSTANCE
  opt --host
    Note over GW: Use the named hosts<br/>up to ten, exact set
  end
  Note over GW: Validate, plan hosts<br/>tracking Routes provisioning
  GW->>SW: Copy the Plausible login<br/>to the vault
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the run gets the vault key name, never the credentials; a missing login stops the command before any task starts
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-analytics-enable-direct
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
  SW->>P: Converge the site<br/>@nckrtl/analytics-site · site
  %%> Why:
  %%> - creates the site when it is missing and updates it otherwise, never a duplicate; it sets the timezone and goals and logs out, also after a failure
  opt tracking host served by a Router
    SW->>N: Request the certificate<br/>CSR for the tracking host
    SW->>GW: Sign the CSR<br/>operation:direct:certificate-sign
    %%> Why a call to the Gateway:
    %%> - certificate signing is the one allowed step-to-Gateway call; the Orbit CA stays in the Gateway
    GW-->>SW: Signed certificate<br/>installed on the Router
  end
  SW->>N: Publish Caddy, reload<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/file · reload
  %%> Why one step:
  %%> - sites of hosts you left out go in the same validated reload
  SW->>N: Probe the tracking host<br/>TLS · GET /js/script.js
  opt host outside the TLD
    Note over SW: Publish private DNS<br/>VPN Node over @swamp/ssh
    %%> Why only outside the TLD:
    %%> - private DNS answers the whole TLD, so a host inside it needs no record
  end
  alt every step succeeds
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    Note over GW: Tracking Routes active<br/>site binding saved
    %%> Result:
    %%> - removed hosts' Routes are deleted
  else a step fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    Note over GW: Mark the Routes failed<br/>task failed
    %%> On the Nodes:
    %%> - finished steps stay; a Plausible site already created stays and a rerun reuses it; there is no rollback
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the same command again; it converges the same site and hosts
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
